WEBVTT

1.1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.843
Welcome students.

1.2
00:00:07.843 --> 00:00:15.687
Today we are diving into the fundamentals of nutrition, specifically focusing on how we evaluate the quality of proteins in our diet.

1.3
00:00:15.687 --> 00:00:23.530
Understanding why certain proteins are superior to others is a favorite topic for U P S C C M S and MBBS professional exams.

2.1
00:00:23.530 --> 00:00:30.750
Look at the screen.

2.2
00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:37.970
We are analyzing why egg proteins are considered the best among all food proteins.

2.3
00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:45.190
We need to evaluate four specific criteria, biological value, digestibility, essential amino acid profile, and calorie content to find the correct combination.

3.1
00:00:45.190 --> 00:00:52.897
First, let us discuss Biological Value.

3.2
00:00:52.897 --> 00:01:00.603
This is the proportion of absorbed protein from a food which is retained by the body for growth and maintenance.

3.3
00:01:00.603 --> 00:01:08.310
Eggs have a biological value of nearly one hundred percent, making them the reference standard against which all other proteins are measured.

4.1
00:01:08.310 --> 00:01:16.120
For a protein to be high quality, it must be complete.

4.2
00:01:16.120 --> 00:01:23.930
This means it contains all nine essential amino acids in the correct proportions required by the human body.

4.3
00:01:23.930 --> 00:01:31.740
Egg proteins are complete proteins, ensuring that no limiting amino acid hinders protein synthesis in the liver and muscles.

5.1
00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:39.550
Even a protein with a great amino acid profile is useless if the body cannot absorb it.

5.2
00:01:39.550 --> 00:01:47.360
Digestibility refers to the percentage of nitrogen absorbed from the gut.

5.3
00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:55.170
Egg proteins are highly soluble and easily broken down by gastric and pancreatic enzymes, leading to superior absorption rates.

6.1
00:01:55.170 --> 00:02:01.353
Now, let us look at statement four regarding calorie content.

6.2
00:02:01.353 --> 00:02:07.535
While eggs provide energy, the quality of a protein is never judged by its calories.

6.3
00:02:07.535 --> 00:02:13.718
In fact, proteins provide four calories per gram regardless of the source.

6.4
00:02:13.718 --> 00:02:19.900
Higher calories do not make a protein better, amino acid quality does.

7.1
00:02:19.900 --> 00:02:29.695
Since biological value, digestibility, and the presence of all essential amino acids are all correct, but calorie content is irrelevant to protein quality, statements one, two, and three are the winners.

7.2
00:02:29.695 --> 00:02:39.490
Therefore, the correct option is B.

8.1
00:02:39.490 --> 00:02:57.930
In clinical practice, when managing patients with severe protein energy malnutrition or those recovering from major surgery, we prioritize high biological value proteins like eggs and milk to ensure rapid tissue repair and immune recovery.

9.1
00:02:57.930 --> 00:03:04.597
To remember this for your exam, just think of BDE for Best Digestible Eggs.

9.2
00:03:04.597 --> 00:03:11.263
B for Biological value, D for Digestibility, and E for Essential amino acids.

9.3
00:03:11.263 --> 00:03:17.930
If you see these three, you know you are dealing with a gold standard protein.

10.1
00:03:17.930 --> 00:03:23.308
When you see multiple statement questions, always look for the outlier.

10.2
00:03:23.308 --> 00:03:28.685
In this case, calorie content is a distractor.

10.3
00:03:28.685 --> 00:03:34.062
In nutrition questions, always distinguish between the quantity of energy and the quality of the nutrient.

10.4
00:03:34.062 --> 00:03:39.440
This will save you from choosing the wrong option.

11.1
00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:47.855
For further reading, refer to Park s Textbook of Preventive and Social Medicine under the Nutrition chapter.

11.2
00:03:47.855 --> 00:03:56.270
You will find detailed tables comparing the biological values of various animal and plant proteins.

12.1
00:03:56.270 --> 00:04:02.143
To wrap up, egg proteins are superior because they are complete, highly digestible, and have the highest biological value.

12.2
00:04:02.143 --> 00:04:08.017
Remember that caloric value is not a measure of protein quality.

12.3
00:04:08.017 --> 00:04:13.890
Keep studying and stay focused.
